      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The endorsed candidate secured a decisive popular mandate, ending the long-serving incumbent's bid for a fifth term. This outcome, sealed by the commander-in-chief's decisive endorsement, constitutes a historic disruption to the party's continuity, as the senator became the first from Texas to lose renomination since 1970. The victory, which overcame the opponent's greater fundraising, re-established order within the party.",
